====================================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE BIAS:  M(beta)/M(beta=0) from the spherical Jeans
          equation with the measured two-asymptote beta(r)
====================================================================================================

  THE DERIVATION (closed form):  the spherical Jeans equation
    d(rho sigma_r^2)/dr + 2 beta rho sigma_r^2 / r = -rho G M(r)/r^2
  ->  M_beta(r) = M_0(r) - 2 beta(r) r sigma_r^2(r) / G,  so
    M_beta/M_0 = 1 - 2 beta(r) sigma_r^2(r) r / (G M_0(r))
  (beta > 0 = radial anisotropy: the isotropic inversion OVERESTIMATES)
  The projected estimators operate on sigma_los(R); since
  sigma_los ~ sqrt(M) f(beta) at fixed (M, R/R500), the aperture
  correction is
    q(R) = M(beta)/M(beta=0) = [sigma_los(R; beta=0)/sigma_los(R; beta)]^2
  on the committed NFW c500 = 4.5 forward model (G203/G206 machinery).
  local Jeans M(beta)/M(0) @ R500:  1.0000   (beta(R500) = +0.000, sigma_r^2 r/GM = 0.330)   [beta = 0 (isotropic, the committed reference)]
  local Jeans M(beta)/M(0) @ R500:  0.9536   (beta(R500) = +0.064, sigma_r^2 r/GM = 0.365)   [measured two-asymptote (G209 E1: 0.033->0.560)]
  local Jeans M(beta)/M(0) @ R500:  0.9919   (beta(R500) = +0.011, sigma_r^2 r/GM = 0.355)   [measured piecewise (G209 E2, free, PRIMARY)]
  local Jeans M(beta)/M(0) @ R500:  0.8344   (beta(R500) = +0.198, sigma_r^2 r/GM = 0.418)   [G170 prediction (0.783, 1.72)]
  local Jeans M(beta)/M(0) @ R500:  0.5213   (beta(R500) = +0.500, sigma_r^2 r/GM = 0.479)   [constant SIS-class beta = 0.5 (reference only)]

  profile                                      R= 0.5  R= 1.0  R= 1.5  R= 2.0  R= 3.0  R= 5.0  
  q = M(beta)/M(0): beta = 0 (reference)                           1.0000   1.0000   1.0000   1.0000   1.0000   1.0000 
  q = M(beta)/M(0): measured two-asymptote (E1)                    0.9469   0.8911   0.8458   0.8316   0.8537   1.1327 
  q = M(beta)/M(0): measured piecewise (E2)                        0.9122   0.8816   0.9419   0.8911   1.0260   1.2940 
  q = M(beta)/M(0): G170 prediction (0.783,1.72)                   0.9001   0.8850   0.9155   0.9766   1.0688   1.2232 
  q = M(beta)/M(0): constant SIS-class 0.5                         1.0053   1.0633   1.0759   1.1006   1.1055   1.1374 

  THE OPERATIVE NUMBERS at R/R500 = 1 (the M500 aperture):
    measured two-asymptote (E1): q = 0.8911  (local Jeans 0.9536)
    measured piecewise (E2)    : q = 0.8816  (local Jeans 0.9919)
    G170 prediction            : q = 0.8850
    constant SIS-class 0.5     : q = 1.0633 (NOT the measured shape: the measured beta(r) RISES from 0, so the operative correction is the rising-profile value)

  q error from the G209 cluster-bootstraps (at R500):
    E1 two-asymptote refits: q = 0.8911 +- 0.0045 (n = 100 draws)
    E2 piecewise refits    : q = 0.8816 +- 0.0315 (n = 100 draws)
    combined (inverse-variance): q = 0.8909 +- 0.0045; incl. the E1-E2 estimator systematic +- 0.0047 -> q = 0.8909 +- 0.0065

