====================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE VERDICTS
====================================================================================================
  V1: THE MASS-BIAS CORRECTION: M(beta)/M(beta=0) at the M500 aperture with the measured two-asymptote beta(r) (0.033 -> 0.560, G209 E1) is q = 0.891 +- 0.005 (E1; local Jeans closed form 0.954; E2 piecewise 0.882 +- 0.032, combined 0.891 +- 0.007 incl. the estimator systematic) -- DIRECTION DOWN: the isotropic (beta = 0) reading of the committed HSE masses OVERESTIMATES the Jeans-solved mass by 12.2% (E1) / 13.4% (E2); the corrected M500-class falls from the median 5.655 x1e14 to 5.039 x1e14.  The bias is a systematic of the DYNAMICAL (Jeans/virial) reading of the HSE masses -- the gas-pressure hydrostatics themselves (the X-ray M_FORW) carry no anisotropy term; the correction applies to the sector's use of M500 as the virial/Jeans M_dyn.

  V2: THE RE-RUN CLOSURES vs THE ORIGINALS: (a) 2/3 temperature law: cluster residual scatter 0.052 -> 0.052 dex (INVARIANT, the shape survives); rms about zero 0.067 -> 0.092 dex; the zero-parameter mean offset +0.042 -> +0.076 dex absorbs the bias; pointwise alpha 0.75 -> 0.81 (2/3 drifts from 0.7 sigma to 1.1 sigma away -- the one soft face, still inside 2 sigma).  (b) pie: s_b 17.7% -> 19.8%, s_ph 56.9% -> 63.9%, s_d 24.6% -> 15.4% (the phantom:baryon ratio INVARIANT to 1e-9; the dust remainder absorbs the bias; negative-dust 1 -> 1/12).  (c) saturation: M_sat 3.09 -> 2.75 x1e14, relative position log10(M_min/M_sat) +0.052 -> +0.052 (INVARIANT).  (d) outer slope: dark residual -2.17 -> -2.22 and total -2.22 (exactly invariant), still in the theory band [-2.4,-2.0] with NFW -3 at 2.4 sigma; the G108 (r_M,R500) dust envelope softens -2.38 -> -2.29 (still in-band), while the (600,R500) concat dust-envelope face flattens -2.28 -> -1.35 (normalization-sensitive subtraction -- the envelope face's honest limit).  VERDICT: the closures survive in their ratio/shape/frame forms (4/4); the absolute levels and one subtraction-sensitive face move by the bias amplitude.

  V3: THE HONEST STATEMENT: the anisotropy correction is a REAL re-scaling of the cluster sector's ABSOLUTE masses -- the measured beta(r) (0.03 -> 0.56) lowers the Jeans-solved M500 by the median factor q = 0.891 (E1) / 0.882 (E2), a 9-13% systematic with a definite direction (the isotropic reading overestimates) -- AND it is SIMULTANEOUSLY a frame-preserving shift: because the beta(r) is a STACK quantity, the correction is a UNIFORM multiplicative factor, and the sector's ratios/exponents/frames are invariant: the 2/3 law's residual scatter (0.052 dex), the phantom:baryon ratio (exactly), the saturation's relative position (exactly), the total density's outer slope (exactly), the dark-residual outer-slope class (-2.2, in-band, NFW still rejected), the f-slope d log10 f/d log10 M500 and the u(M500) exponent.  What MOVES is the absolute bookkeeping: the T-law's zero-parameter mean offset (+0.033 dex) and the pointwise alpha's drift (0.75 -> 0.81, 2/3 now 1.1 sigma away, the one soft face), the pie's dust share (-9.2 points), M_sat's absolute position (3.09 -> 2.75 x1e14), and the (600,R500) dust-ENVELOPE outer-slope concat (-2.28 -> -1.35, out of band -- the subtraction face is normalization-sensitive; the G108 (r_M,R500) envelope only softens to -2.29, in-band).  The precise honest framing: the correction SHIFTS the cluster sector's absolute masses by a measured, direction-fixed factor, leaves every ratio/frame and the model-independent shape tests intact, and re-anchors the absolute levels and one subtraction-sensitive face by the bias amplitude -- it is NOT a restructuring of the sector, and it is NOT negligible for any single absolute mass statement (M_sat, the dust share, the T-law's constant).

  [PASS] V1 [the mass-bias correction] the median factor and direction measured
         measured: q = 0.8911 +- 0.0045 (E1) / 0.8816 +- 0.0315 (E2), direction DOWN (10.9% overestimate by the isotropic reading)
         reading : the median correction: q ~ 0.89 (E1), direction down; the corrected M500-class is 11% (E1) / 13% (E2) lighter than the committed HSE reading.
  [PASS] V2 [the re-run closures vs the originals] all four relations survive in ratio/shape/frame form with the absolute levels re-anchored
         measured: T-law scatter 0.052->0.052; pie s_d 25%->15%; M_sat 3.09->2.75; outer slope -2.17->-2.22 in-band
         reading : the closures' SHAPE is invariant by construction (uniform factor); their ABSOLUTE levels move by the bias amplitude -- the re-run is a re-anchoring, not a break.
  [PASS] V3 [the honest statement] a systematic that shifts the absolute masses but leaves the ratios/frames intact -- or a real re-scaling with consequences?
         measured: THE HONEST STATEMENT: the anisotropy correction is a REAL re-scaling of the cluster sector's ABSOLUTE masses -- the measured beta(r) (0.03 -> 0.56) lowers the Jeans-solved M500 by the median factor q = 0.891 (E1) / 0.882 (E2), a 9-13% systematic with a definite direction (the isotropic reading overestimates) -- AND it is SIMULTANEOUSLY a frame-preserving shift: because the beta(r) is a STACK quantity, the correction is a UNIFORM multiplicative factor, and the sector's ratios/exponents/frames are invariant: the 2/3 law's residual scatter (0.052 dex), the phantom:baryon ratio (exactly), the saturation's relative position (exactly), the total density's outer slope (exactly), the dark-residual outer-slope class (-2.2, in-band, NFW still rejected), the f-slope d log10 f/d log10 M500 and the u(M500) exponent.  What MOVES is the absolute bookkeeping: the T-law's zero-parameter mean offset (+0.033 dex) and the pointwise alpha's drift (0.75 -> 0.81, 2/3 now 1.1 sigma away, the one soft face), the pie's dust share (-9.2 points), M_sat's absolute position (3.09 -> 2.75 x1e14), and the (600,R500) dust-ENVELOPE outer-slope concat (-2.28 -> -1.35, out of band -- the subtraction face is normalization-sensitive; the G108 (r_M,R500) envelope only softens to -2.29, in-band).  The precise honest framing: the correction SHIFTS the cluster sector's absolute masses by a measured, direction-fixed factor, leaves every ratio/frame and the model-independent shape tests intact, and re-anchors the absolute levels and one subtraction-sensitive face by the bias amplitude -- it is NOT a restructuring of the sector, and it is NOT negligible for any single absolute mass statement (M_sat, the dust share, the T-law's constant).
